<DocPage
	eyebrow="About"
	title="About HippOS"
	description="A Debian-based console-style gaming OS built around a controller-first frontend."
>
	<p>
		HippOS is a console-style gaming OS for handhelds and living-room PCs. The goal is simple: boot into a
		gaming-first experience where Linux is the platform underneath, not something you have to manage.
	</p>
	<p>
		Flash the image, plug in a controller, and you're in EmulationStation. Your ROMs, saves, BIOS files and configs
		live on their own partition, so updating the OS never touches them.
	</p>

	<h2>Design principles</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Frontend-first:</strong> boot straight into a console-like experience, with no desktop to navigate.</li>
		<li><strong>Controller-first:</strong> normal use never needs a keyboard or mouse.</li>
		<li><strong>Gaming-first:</strong> launching, configuring and keeping your games safe comes before everything else.</li>
		<li><strong>Modular:</strong> the OS, emulators, frontend and your data are separate and update independently.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Status</h2>
	<p>
		HippOS is in public beta, with regular releases shaped by tester reports. See the <a href="/changelog">changelog</a>
		for what's changed recently and <a href="/hardware">Hardware</a> for what's known to work.
	</p>

	<h2>Get involved</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>Testers:</strong> flash the image, boot it on your hardware, and report what breaks in the
		<a href="/discord">Discord</a>.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Developers:</strong> the stack is Debian, Bash, Python, a C++ EmulationStation fork, and Astro for this site.
		Issues and pull requests are welcome on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>.
	</p>
</DocPage>
